Hopfield Memory
A from-scratch Hopfield network that stores 7x7 letter bitmaps and restores them from
noisy copies.
How it works
Learning: Hebbian rule, W = (1/N) Σ p pᵀ with the diagonal zeroed.
Recall: asynchronous updates in random order until a full sweep changes nothing.
Energy: E = -½ sᵀWs — it only goes down, so the network always settles.
Run
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate # macOS/Linux: source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python run_demo.py --noise 0.2
python -m pytest
Layout
hopfield/network.py core model
hopfield/patterns.py letters + noise helpers
